{"In-proc server interceptor sets auth namespace to '*' enabling cross-namespace checks - by injecting auth info with namespace '*' for the inproc channel, any in-process caller can request permissions for any namespace and bypass per-namespace restriction checks": 0.11043564230203629, "Denial cache entries cannot be invalidated causing stale false-denies - permDenialCache is written on deny but cacheWrap exposes no Delete method, so users granted new permissions will be incorrectly denied for the entire cache window": 0.8212753534317017, "Ambiguous cache key construction with collision risk - cache keys use underscore separators without escaping, so distinct tuples like userUID='a_b'/action='c' vs userUID='a'/action='b_c' can produce identical keys": 0.5259352326393127, "Denial cache used only for Check but not List leading to inconsistent responses - Check consults permDenialCache to return deny for specific resources, but List does not consult it, causing potential inconsistency where List reports a resource is visible but Check denies access": 0.38543251156806946, "Refactored cache lookup causes unnecessary DB calls on cache hits - early permCache check was removed from getUserPermissions/getAnonymousPermissions, and getCachedIdentityPermissions still calls GetUserIdentifiers potentially hitting the DB even when permissions are cached": 0.576054573059082}